//! Every official Managed request shape must decode into the exact route
//! parameter type this server uses for that operation.
//!
//! The corpus is `contracts/request-witnesses.generated.json`, generated by
//! `@awaken/managed-sdk-oracle` from the current official TypeScript SDK: for
//! each operation the exact wire request (query pairs and JSON/multipart body)
//! the SDK emits for a required-only invocation, an every-optional invocation,
//! and every union member. This module maps each operation id to the decoder
//! the handler really runs (the same serde type behind `ManagedJson<T>` /
//! `ManagedQuery<T>`, the same hand-written query parser, the same surface
//! selector) and decodes every witness through it.
//!
//! Cause/effect: C1 an operation exists in the corpus; C2 it has a registry
//! row; C3 every witness decodes through that row. Effects: E1 pass; E2 fail
//! naming the unmapped operation (no silent skip); E3 fail naming the
//! operation, witness id, and serde error. Rules: C1+!C2 -> E2; C1+C2+!C3 ->
//! E3; a registry row whose operation left the corpus -> E2 (stale mapping).
//!
//! This is the gate commit c4f378c08 lacked: it replaced the official memory
//! `precondition` body with an internal generation witness and made memory
//! delete demand `expected_version`; every official SDK then got 400 for
//! weeks because only a release e2e could observe it. The named decision
//! rows at the bottom pin exactly those two shapes.

